The constraints are:
$1 \le num1 \le num2 \le 10^{22}$
$1 \le min\_sum \le max\_sum \le 400$

The numbers can be very large (up to $10^{22}$), so we cannot iterate through all numbers. This suggests a Digit DP approach.
The condition $num1 \le x \le num2$ can be split into two parts:
1. Count integers $x$ such that $0 \le x \le num2$ and $min\_sum \le \text{digit\_sum}(x) \le max\_sum$.
2. Count integers $x$ such that $0 \le x \le num1 - 1$ and $min\_sum \le \text{digit\_sum}(x) \le max\_sum$.
The answer will be (count for $num2$) - (count for $num1 - 1$).

